tanding of <italic>Coxiella burnetii</italic> infection in Japan</article-title><source>J Vet Med Sci</source><year>1998</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>781</fpage><lpage>790</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9713803</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tissot-Dupont</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Raoult</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Brouqui</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Janbon</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Peyramond</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiller</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Chicheportiche</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Nezri</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Poirier</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epidemiologic features and clinical presentation of acute Q fever in hospitalized patients; 323 French cases</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>1992</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>427</fpage><lpage>434</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1415306</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Raoult</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Q fever: still a query after all these years</article-title><source>J Med Microbiol</source><year>1996</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>77</fpage><lpage>78</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8642579</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>WY</given-names></name></person-group><a